PHASE 3N.2 — GW2 REALITY, PLAYER-ROLE & USER-DECISION AUDIT

OBJECTIVE

This is the FINAL DIAGNOSTIC / CORRECTION PHASE before the system is
allowed to make an actual GW2 FPL decision.

The project has accumulated a large number of successful tests, but the
live frontend has demonstrated that passing internal consistency tests
does NOT necessarily mean the decision engine is producing useful FPL
decisions.

The purpose of this phase is therefore:

MAKE THE DECISION ENGINE ACTUALLY USEFUL FOR A REAL FPL DECISION.

We need to verify that the system understands:

- what gameweek we are actually in
- which players are actually available
- who is actually likely to start
- current clubs
- current fixtures
- recent performance
- historical performance
- transfer uncertainty
- injuries
- expected minutes
- current prices
- the difference between current role and historical ability
- the user's actual squad
- the user's actual transfer/chip constraints
- the difference between immediate and multi-GW optimization

This phase MUST NOT blindly trust previous "PASS" results.

Where a previous test only proved internal consistency, this phase must
test external/current-state correctness.

