PART 6 — EXPECTED-MINUTES AUDIT
==================================================

This is one of the most important parts of the entire phase.

The current engine has previously produced suspiciously similar expected
minutes values for players with very different role situations.

For example, investigate any clustering around values such as:

75.0 minutes

Do NOT assume 75 is wrong.

Determine whether it is:

- a genuine model output
- a default
- a fallback
- a midpoint
- a hard-coded assumption
- a consequence of missing role data

For every player with exactly 75.0 expected minutes:

report the underlying calculation and source features.

If 75 is a fallback caused by missing information:

FIX THE FALLBACK.

Do not hide the issue.

